cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "libmatern: the normalised Matérn covariance function in double precision"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Mann"
    given-names: "Daniel"
    affiliation: "Chair of Applied Stochastics, University of Mannheim"
  - family-names: "Ehrhardt"
    given-names: "Matthis"
    affiliation: "Chair of Applied Stochastics, University of Mannheim"
  - family-names: "Schlather"
    given-names: "Martin"
    affiliation: "Chair of Applied Stochastics, University of Mannheim"
version: "0.9.0"
date-released: 2026-10-10
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/DanielMann27/libmatern"
abstract: >-
  The normalised Matérn covariance function in double precision, with vectorised
  backends for AVX-512 and AVX2, a width-1 build of the same kernels for CPUs
  without AVX2, an independent scalar implementation to test against, and a
  CUDA backend. The (nu, z) plane is partitioned into regions, each evaluated by
  an approximation of the modified Bessel function K_nu, in most regions with the
  covariance prefactor folded in.
keywords:
  - Matérn covariance
  - Whittle-Matérn
  - modified Bessel function
  - SIMD
  - CUDA
references:
  - type: dataset
    title: "Reference high precision datasets for the Matérn covariance function"
